Assume that $\underline{v}$ is a subsolution (resp. $\overline{v}$ is a supersolution) of equation
(\ref{eq::1ter}) on $[0,T)$ such that
$$\underline{v}(0,x)\le \overline{v}(0,x)\quad \mbox{for all}\quad  x\in {\mathbb R}.$$
Then
$$\underline{v}\le \overline{v}\quad \mbox{on}\quad  [0,T)\times {\mathbb R}.$$
