\label{prop-weak-comparison}{\bf (Weak maximum principle).}
Let $u\in H$ be a weak supersolution of \eqref{weak-equation} with $g\equiv 0$, and let $d(x)$ be a measurable bounded function. Set $u=P*_x w$. Assume that $u\geq 0$ in $\overline{B_R^+}$, and that $d>0$ on $\mathbb R\backslash[-R,R]$. Then
$$u\geq 0 \quad\mbox{in }\mathbb R^2_+,$$
and also, $Tu\geq 0$ on $\mathbb R$.
\label{prop-moser-iteration}{\bf ($L^\infty$ bound for $g=0$).}
Let $w\in H^{\frac{1}{2}}(\mathbb R)$ be a weak subsolution of \eqref{weak-equation} with $g\equiv 0$ for some uniformly bounded  function $d$ defined on $\mathbb R$.
Then
$$\sup_{\mathbb R} w\leq C \norm{w^+}_{L^2(\mathbb R)}.$$
If $w$ is a supersolution, the conclusion reads
$$\sup_{\mathbb R} \{-w\}\leq C \norm{w^-}_{L^2(\mathbb R)}.$$
The constant does not depend on $w$.
