In Fig.~\ref{fig:PSNRn}, we examine the impact of number of channels $N$.  We increase $N$ from 3 to 15 in steps of 3, and plot the average PSNR values of all multicast users. As expected, the more channels, the more spectrum opportunities for the CR networks, and the better the video quality.  Again, we observe that the Greedy Algorithm curve has the steepest slope, implying it is more efficient in exploiting the increased spectrum opportunity for video transmissions. 


