Let $G$ be a totally disconnected locally compact group, $\phi:G\to G$ a topological automorphism and $U\in\mathcal B(G)$. Then 
$$H_{top}(\phi,U)=\log[\phi^{-1}(C(\phi,U)):C(\phi,U)]+\log\Delta(\phi).$$
\label{basesuff}
Let $G$ be a totally disconnected locally compact group, $\phi:G\to G$ a continuous endomorphism and $\mathcal B\subseteq \mathcal B(G)$ a local base at $1$. Then $h_{top}(\phi)=\sup\{H_{top}(\phi,U):U\in\mathcal B\}$.
Lemma \ref{logalpha} yields that the limit defining the topological entropy exists, and gives a precise description for the value of the topological entropy $H_{top}(\phi,U)$ of a topological automorphism $\phi:G\to G$ of a totally disconnected locally compact group $G$ with respect to $U\in\mathcal B(G)$; in particular, this value is in $\log\mathbb N_+$, so the value $h_{top}(\phi)\in\log\mathbb N_+\cup\{\infty\}$.

