{\rm\cite{Ccm01,Sico03}}
Let $\ensuremath{{\mathcal X}}$ be a reflexive real Banach space and let 
$f\colon\ensuremath{{\mathcal X}}\to\ensuremath{\left]-\infty,+\infty\right]}$ be a proper lower semicontinuous convex function,
with conjugate $f^*\colon\ensuremath{{\mathcal X}}^*\to\ensuremath{\left]-\infty,+\infty\right]}\colon
x^*\mapsto\sup_{x\in\ensuremath{{\mathcal X}}}(\pair{x}{x^*}-f(x))$ and 
Moreau subdifferential \cite{Mor63c}
\begin{equation}
\label{e:subdiff}
\partial f\colon\ensuremath{{\mathcal X}}\to 2^{\ensuremath{{\mathcal X}}^*}\colon x\mapsto
\menge{x^*\in\ensuremath{{\mathcal X}}^*}{(\forall y\in\ensuremath{{\mathcal X}})\,
\pair{y-x}{x^*}+f(x)\ensuremath{\leqslant} f(y)}.  
\end{equation}
Then $f$ is a \emph{Legendre function} if it is 
\emph{essentially smooth} in the sense that $\partial f$ is 
both locally bounded and single-valued on its
domain, and \emph{essentially strictly convex} in the sense
that $\partial f^*$ is locally bounded on its domain and 
$f$ is strictly convex on every convex subset of $\ensuremath{\text{\rm dom}\,}\partial f$.
Moreover, $f$ is G\^ateaux differentiable on $\ensuremath{\text{\rm int\:dom}f}\neq\ensuremath{{\varnothing}}$
and the associated \emph{Bregman distance} is 
\begin{equation}
\label{e:Bdist}
\begin{aligned}
D^f\colon\ensuremath{{\mathcal X}}\times\ensuremath{{\mathcal X}}&\to\,[0,\ensuremath{{+\infty}}]\\
(x,y)&\mapsto 
\begin{cases}
f(x)-f(y)-\pair{x-y}{\nabla f(y)},&\text{if}\;\;y\in\ensuremath{\text{\rm int\:dom}f};\\
\ensuremath{{+\infty}},&\text{otherwise}.
\end{cases}
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
Let $C$ be a closed convex subset of $\ensuremath{{\mathcal X}}$ such that
$C\cap\ensuremath{\text{\rm int\:dom}f}\neq\ensuremath{{\varnothing}}$. The \emph{Bregman projector} onto $C$ induced
by $f$ is 
\begin{equation}
\label{e:2001}
\begin{aligned}
P^f_C\colon\ensuremath{\text{\rm int\:dom}f}&\to C\cap\ensuremath{\text{\rm int\:dom}f}\\
y&\mapsto\underset{x\in C}{\text{argmin}}\,D^f(x,y).
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}

