  \end{displaymath}
  and
  \begin{displaymath}
    S_{nj}:=\{\tau_{nj}(x)^{-1}x:\; x\in W_{nj}\}.

A random element $\xi$ in $\mathbb{K}$ is said to be \emph{strictly
  $\alpha$-stable} if
\begin{equation}
  \label{Eq:stable}
  a^{1/\alpha}\xi'+b^{1/\alpha}\xi''
  \overset{d}{\sim} (a+b)^{1/\alpha}\xi\,,\qquad a,b>0\,,
\end{equation}
where $\xi'$ and $\xi''$ are i.i.d. copies of $\xi$.

Let $\tilde{\bK}$ be the countable family of characters
