 \item[(2)] $A$ is a non-local weakly symmetric algebra of Euclidean type if and only if $A$ is isomorphic to an algebra of the form $\Lambda (T,v_1,v_2)$, $\Lambda'(T)$, $\Gamma^{(0)}(T,v)$, $\Gamma^{(1)}(T,v)$, or $\Gamma^{(2)}(T,v_1,v_2)$.
