\label{D main result}
Assume that $\cha K\neq 2$.
\begin{enumerate}
\item Let $A$ be a basic $K$-algebra of infinite type. Then the following are equivalent.
\begin{enumerate}
\item $A$ is a standard domestic self-injective cellular algebra.
\item $A$ is isomorphic to one of the algebras 
$K[X,Y]/(X^2, Y^2)$, $\Lambda'(T(0,1))$, $\Gamma^{(0)}(T(1),v)$, 
$\Lambda(T,v_{1},v_{2})$ where $T$ is a straight line, or $\Gamma^{(2)}(T_{l}^{0},v_1,v_2)$ for $l\in\{-1,0\}$.
\end{enumerate}

\item There is no non-standard domestic self-injective cellular algebra.
\end{enumerate}
