Experiment 1: Quality of the Proposed Method
In the first experiment we empirically examine the size of a separator
obtained by our proposed algorithm
with the modification proposed at the beginning of this section.

For random instances, we fix $L=100$, and vary the number of disks $n$ 
from $10,000$ to $30,000$ with an increment of $50$.
Since our algorithm is randomized, we run the algorithm $k$ times, where
$k\in \{1, 2, 10, 15, 20\}$, and compute the average separator size (because of Theorem~\ref{thm:joint_unit}, we expect the average to converge to $O(\sqrt{m\log n})$ as $k$ grows to infinity).

\begin{figure}[t]
  \centering
  \resizebox{.4\textwidth}{!}{\includegraphics{random_sep_k_1.pdf}}
  \resizebox{.4\textwidth}{!}{\includegraphics{random_sep_k_2.pdf}}
