  }
  \label{fig:exp1-1}
\end{figure}

\begin{figure}[t]
  \centering
  \resizebox{0.8\textwidth}{!}{\includegraphics{comp_fox_opt_random2.pdf}}
  \caption{
    Comparison of the separator sizes of our method with the Fox-Pach method
    for random instances.
    The horizontal axis shows the number of edges, and 
    the vertical axis shows the separator size;
    the red bar is obtained by the Fox-Pach method,
    the blue bar is an optimal line separator, 
    and the remaining four bars are obtained by our method after trying $k$ 
    random directions  ($k\in \{1,5,50,100\}$) and returning the minimum
    size separators. For all methods we repeat this process 20 times and
    display the average minimum size. 
