Let $\eta\in W^{k-1,2,\delta,\delta}(\tilde C_\alpha,\Omega^{0,1}_{\tilde C_\alpha,j_y}\otimes_\mathbb C u_\alpha^\ast TM_{J(\ell_{\alpha,w}(A_y(\cdot)))})$.  Away from the ends with $\alpha\ne 0$, $\operatorname{break}(\eta)$ is given by $(\operatorname{id}^{1,0})^{-1}(\eta)$, where $\operatorname{id}^{1,0}:TM_{J(\ell_{0,0}(A_y(\cdot)))}\to TM_{J(\ell_{\alpha,w}(A_y(\cdot)))}$ denotes the $(1,0)$-component of the identity map.  In any particular bubble end $[0,\infty)\times S^1\subseteq C_0$ with $\alpha\ne 0$, we define:
