There is canonical homeomorphism $\overline{\mathcal M}(\sigma,p,q)^{S^1}=\overline{\mathcal M}_\mathrm{morse}(\sigma,p,q)$.
\label{morseistransverse}
Fix a Morse function $H_0:M\to\mathbb R$ whose gradient flow is Morse--Smale and suppose $H=\epsilon\cdot H_0$ with $\epsilon>0$ sufficiently small.  Then $\overline{\mathcal M}(\sigma,p,q)^{S^1}\subseteq\overline{\mathcal M}(\sigma,p,q)$ is open and cut out transversally (meaning $\overline{\mathcal M}(\sigma,p,q)^{S^1}\subseteq\overline{\mathcal M}(\sigma,p,q)^\mathrm{reg}$).  Hence we have a partition into disjoint closed subsets:
\begin{equation}
\overline{\mathcal M}(\sigma,p,q)=\overline{\mathcal M}(\sigma,p,q)^{S^1}\sqcup[\overline{\mathcal M}(\sigma,p,q)\setminus\overline{\mathcal M}(\sigma,p,q)^{S^1}]
