These two properties imply that $\operatornamewithlimits{hocolim}_{I\subseteq J\subseteq A}(\mathcal G_{IJ})_p$ is simply $\mathcal G_p$ tensored with the simplicial chain complex of the nerve of $(2^A)_p$ (which is contractible).  Hence \eqref{FGiso} gives a canonical isomorphism of stalks $H^0\mathcal F^\bullet_p=\mathcal G_p$ (and thus in particular $\mathcal F^\bullet$ is pure).

Now it remains to construct a canonical isomorphism of sheaves $\mathcal G\xrightarrow\sim H^0\mathcal F^\bullet$.  Over the open set $U_I$, we define this isomorphism to be the composition $\mathcal G_{II}\xrightarrow\sim H^0\mathcal F_{II}^\bullet\to H^0\mathcal F^\bullet$ (the second map being the inclusion of a $p=0$ subcomplex in the homotopy colimit).  At any point $p\in U_I$, this specializes to the isomorphism of stalks $\mathcal G_p=H^0\mathcal F^\bullet_p$ defined earlier.  Hence since $\{U_I\}_{I\subseteq A}$ is an open cover of $X$, these isomorphisms patch together to give the desired global isomorphism.

