denote the derivative of $\mathcal F_{\alpha,y,\zeta}$ at zero.  Of course, $D_{\alpha,y,\zeta}$ may be calculated as in Lemma \ref{linearizedformula}, and the result is the same (i.e.\ we just substitute $(\exp_{u_\alpha}\zeta,e_0+\operatorname{proj}_E\zeta)$ in place of $(u_\alpha,e_0)$).

Now the first step in proving \eqref{derivislip} is to express $\mathcal F_{\alpha,y}'(\zeta,\xi)$ in terms of $D_{\alpha,y,\zeta}$.  To do this, we observe that:
